WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Moderator: This is a concept for an executive portfolio view. What stands out?

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Naomi Adeyemi: Finally, renewals by quarter and risk by reason on one screen. That's what I ask my team for every week.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Naomi Adeyemi: Showing the reason behind each score helps me trust it. I've never trusted the health score because nobody could explain it.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:06.000
Moderator: What would you do with this?

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:24.000
Naomi Adeyemi: Take it to the board. I'd want a board-ready export with the story: what's at risk, why, and who is on it. Right now my ops manager builds slides by hand.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Naomi Adeyemi: I'd like the weekly digest instead of alerts. Alerts are noise to me. Tell me what changed.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:10.000
Naomi Adeyemi: The thing I care about is that handoffs don't drop. If support escalates and success misses it, we lose a customer. Show me open handoffs.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:29.000
Moderator: What would make you confident in the tool?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Naomi Adeyemi: Fresh data. If a number is two days old I can't use it in a meeting. And the customer timeline, my team loves it, keep it central.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:07.000
Naomi Adeyemi: If I could show that every at-risk renewal has an owner and a plan, that's the story I want to tell.

